             inversion lives in `.band--dark` in styles.css (local custom-property
             overrides — no filters), so the content markup is untouched. */}
        <section id="work" class="band band--dark" aria-labelledby="work-title">
            <div class="band-inner" data-rail="03 / Work">
                <div class="section-head">
                    <h2 id="work-title" class="section-title reveal reveal-clip">Work</h2>
                    <p class="section-intro reveal">The professional stuff, if you're into that.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="section-body">
                    <h3 class="subhead subhead-flush reveal">What I Do</h3>
                    <div class="prose">
                        <p class="reveal">I'm an SDE II at Amazon Lab126. These days I work on the data pipeline for autonomous delivery robots — the C++ software that pulls terabytes of sensor data off the vehicles and into the cloud. Before that I owned the camera stack on Amazon's smart delivery glasses, which mostly meant making cameras crash a whole lot less.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h3 class="subhead reveal">Skills &amp; Tools</h3>
                    <ul class="skills-list reveal">
                        <li>C++ / Python</li>
                        <li>ROS2</li>
                        <li>Embedded Linux</li>
                        <li>Camera Systems / HAL</li>
                        <li>AWS (S3, IoT, KMS)</li>
                        <li>MQTT</li>
                        <li>RAID</li>
                        <li>SED / TCG</li>
                        <li>Edge Computing</li>
                        <li>PyTorch / Keras</li>
                        <li>Docker</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3 class="subhead reveal">Experience</h3>
                    <div class="timeline">
                        {/* Read-progress rail: scrubs from 0 to full as the
                             timeline scrolls past. Rests filled with motion off. */}
                        <span class="timeline-rail" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        {/* GROUPED BY EMPLOYER, the way LinkedIn does it: the company is
                             the anchor, total tenure sits under it, and each rung carries its
                             own dates — but with ONE description for the whole stint rather
                             than one per rung, which is what was asked for.

                             The <h4> is the COMPANY now, not the current title, so the roles
                             can be an ordered list inside the entry instead of competing with
                             it for the same heading level. Newest first, as on a CV. The
                             overall "February 2024 – Present" span is gone: with per-rung
                             dates and a tenure line it was the same fact three times.

                             Durations come from the frontmatter, never typed. */}
                        <article class="exp-item exp-item--grouped reveal" aria-labelledby="exp-lab126-title">
                            <div class="exp-head">
                                <h4 id="exp-lab126-title" class="exp-title">Amazon Lab126</h4>
                                <span class="exp-date">Full-time · {lab126Dur}</span>
                            </div>
                            <ol class="exp-rungs">
                                <li class="exp-rung">
                                    <span class="exp-rung-title">Software Development Engineer II</span>
                                    <span class="exp-rung-date">Jul 2026 – Present · {sde2Dur}</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="exp-rung">
                                    <span class="exp-rung-title">Software Development Engineer I</span>
                                    <span class="exp-rung-date">Feb 2024 – Jul 2026 · {sde1Dur}</span>
                                </li>
                            </ol>
                            <p>Building the high-throughput data pipeline for autonomous delivery robots — a C++ edge appliance that ingests self-encrypting drives of vehicle sensor data into S3, moving 40+ Gbps across drives uploading in parallel. Owns the drive security lifecycle end to end: keyless cloud auth, encrypted-drive unlock, and audited crypto-erase.</p>
                            <p>Before this, was the SME for the camera stack on Amazon's smart delivery glasses — drove camera failure rates from 30.7% down to 0.5% and shipped hardware dewarp that cut CPU ~80%, across 244 devices and 270k+ deliveries.</p>
                        </article>

                        <article class="exp-item reveal" aria-labelledby="exp-intern-title">
                            <div class="exp-head">
                                <h4 id="exp-intern-title" class="exp-title">Software Development Engineer Intern</h4>
                                <span class="exp-date">June 2022 – September 2022</span>
                            </div>
                            <p class="exp-company">Amazon Lab126</p>
                            <p>Architected and trained 10+ two-branch convolutional neural networks on IMU sensor data, achieving 90% accuracy via device-collected data through Keras' functional API and scikit-learn.</p>
                            <p>Implemented 4 models onto the device to perform real-time classification in 1.5 seconds at 90% accuracy using ROS (rospy and roscpp) and an internal API that executes .tflite models in C++.</p>
                        </article>

                        <article class="exp-item reveal" aria-labelledby="exp-tutor-title">
                            <div class="exp-head">
                                <h4 id="exp-tutor-title" class="exp-title">ECE Department Tutor</h4>
                                <span class="exp-date">September 2020 – June 2023</span>
                            </div>
                            <p class="exp-company">UC San Diego, Jacobs School of Engineering</p>
                            <p>Tutored 800+ students with homework and exam preparation over 10 academic quarters across 2 different courses. Achieved 100% recommendation rate from student surveys.</p>
                        </article>
                    </div>

                    {resumeExists ? (
                        <p class="resume-line reveal"><a href={RESUME_PATH} class="btn-resume" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download Résumé <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
                    ) : (
                        <p class="resume-line reveal"><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Résumé request')}`} class="btn-resume">Résumé on request <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
                    )}
